    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0403" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg287"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1714.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-09T08:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 9, 1915—8 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Party of armed men have gone to bush from Macoris and small party got away from
                    here. Leonte Vasquez, brother of Horacio, <pb facs="0404" n="288" xml:id="pg288"
                    /> has recently returned from the United States and is in Puerto Plata. Vidal
                    thought to have left New York City on the <hi rendition="#italic">Iroquois</hi>
                    but if not his activities in New York should be investigated with a view to
                    arrest. The Government has made a considerable number of arrests here and in
                    Puerto Plata of conspirators against the public peace. Enforced enlistment for
                    the army also rigorously proceeding. The Dominican gunboat <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Independencia</hi> has left for northern points.
                    Censorship on cables and telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
